{"extract": "Tanja Tellervo Karpela (née Vienonen; previously Karpela and Saarela; born 22 August 1970) is a Finnish former politician and beauty pageant titleholder who was crowned Miss Finland 1991. She was a Member of Parliament of Finland from 1999 to 2011 and served in the government of Finland as Minister of Culture from 2003 to 2007.", "links": [{"ns": 0, "title": "Anneli Jäätteenmäki", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Finland", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Finnish Centre", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Finnish Parliament", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Kaarina Dromberg", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Matti Vanhanen", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Miss Finland", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Olli Saarela", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Parliament of Finland", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Political party", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Salo, Finland", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Stefan Wallin", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Uusimaa (electoral district)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Finnish Minister of Culture", "exists": false}]}